Trilium Notes
-------------

The Lab Notebook's design follows Trilium Notes (TriliumNext), a hierarchical
note-taking application:

    https://github.com/TriliumNext/Trilium
    Copyright (C) zadam, Elian Doran and other contributors
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0

Taken from Trilium are its ideas, not its source code:

  - notes kept apart from where they sit in the tree (notes and branches), so
    one note can appear in several places ("clones");
  - attributes on notes: labels (#name=value) and relations (~name=@note);
  - a revision kept for every change to a note, folding edits made close
    together into one;
  - day notes filed under their year and month, as in Trilium's journal;
  - internal links between notes, and the notes linking to each one.

The Lab Notebook is a separate program, written for the Gardiner Lab suite in
Python and plain JavaScript. It contains no code copied from Trilium. It is
released under the same licence as Trilium, the AGPL v3.0, so that ideas and,
where useful, code can move between the two.
